        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Medina</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 850 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Medina was inhabited at least 1,500 years before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hijra">Hijra</a> of 622, approximately the 9th century BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> region of western Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, in an oasis on a plateau at about 620 m above sea level, about 250 km from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> coast and about 720 km north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Yathrib before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>; Muhammad's migration of 622; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophets-mosque">Prophet's Mosque</a> and the Quba Mosque; the Battles of Uhud and the Trench; capital of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> railway; the siege of 1916 to 1919</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Medina is the capital of Medina Province in Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, a city of roughly 1.5 million people, and the second holiest city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>.</span></div>
